# Getting Started
Python is a high-level, interpreted programming language known for its simplicity and readability.

# Installation
Install Python from python.org or use a package manager like brew, apt, or conda.

# Python Basics
Learn about variables, data types, operators, and basic syntax in Python.

# Control Flow
Master if statements, for loops, while loops, and conditional logic.

# Functions
Create reusable code blocks with functions using the def keyword.

# Modules & Packages
Organize code using modules and packages. Import using import statement.

# File I/O
Read from and write to files using open(), read(), write() methods.

# Best Practices
Follow PEP 8 style guide, write clean code, use virtual environments.